Here's an example of a SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity Check) encoder for FPGA implementation:
```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in[],
    output wire data_out[]
);

reg [7:0] data_reg[7:0];
reg [3:0] parity_reg[3:0];

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        data_reg <= 8'b00000000;
        parity_reg <= 4'b0000;
    end
    else
    begin
        data_reg <= data_in;
        parity_reg <= parity_calc(data_reg);
        data_out <= concatenate(data_reg, parity_reg);
    end
end

function [7:0] parity_calc(data);
    // Implementation of LDPC parity check algorithm goes here
    // ...
endfunction

endmodule
```
This module implements a simple LDPC encoder with a 8-bit data input and a 4-bit parity output. The `parity_calc` function contains the implementation of the LDPC parity check algorithm. You can replace this function with your own implementation or use a pre-defined LDPC encoder library.

