Certainly! Here's a JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function switchAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word.match(/^[a-zA-Z]+$/)); // Filter out non-alphabetical words

  if (adjectives.length <= 1) {
    return sentence;
  }

  const firstAdjective = adjectives.shift();
  const lastAdjective = adjectives.pop();

  words.splice(words.indexOf(firstAdjective), 0, lastAdjective);
  words.splice(words.indexOf(lastAdjective) + 1, 0, firstAdjective);

  return words.join(" ");
}

const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = switchAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function splits the input sentence into an array of words, filters out non-alphabetical words to find the adjectives, and then swaps the positions of the first and last adjectives in the array. Finally, it joins the words back together to form the output sentence.

