$sql = "SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) as purchase_count
FROM transactions
WHERE product_id = 'specific_product_id' AND date >= DATE_SUB(CURDATE(), INTERVAL 1 WEEK)
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING purchase_count >= 3;";

$result = $conn->query($sql);
?>
```

In this example, we are selecting the customer ID and the number of purchases for each customer who has bought a specific product (with the ID "specific_product_id") within the last week. We then group the results by customer ID and apply the HAVING clause to filter out customers who have made at least three purchases during that time period.

